---
title: Buttermilk Biscuits
description: Tall, flaky buttermilk biscuits, folded like laminated dough.
tags: [biscuits, bread, baking]
course: side
cuisine: American
source:
  name: Serious Eats
  author: J. Kenji López-Alt
  url: https://www.seriouseats.com/the-food-lab-buttermilk-biscuits-recipe
servings: 8
yield: 8%biscuits
time: 35m
why:
  - Cutting the butter into the flour with a food processor ensures that it is incorporated rapidly before it has time to soften or smear.
  - Using a rubber spatula to bring the dough together builds in extra-flaky layers before you even roll.
  - Laminating the dough by folding it over itself a few times delivers even more flaky layers.
---

Adjust an oven rack to the middle position and preheat the oven to 425°F (220°C).

Whisk together the @buttermilk{1/2%cup}(118 ml) and @sour cream{113%g}(1/2 cup) in a #small bowl{}.

In the bowl of a #food processor{}, combine the @all-purpose flour{284%g}(10 oz, plus more for dusting), @baking powder{1%tbsp}, @baking soda{1/4%tsp}, and @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp} and process until blended, about ~process{2%seconds}.

Scatter the @cold unsalted butter{112%g}(8 tbsp, cut into 1/4-inch pats) evenly over the flour and pulse until the mixture resembles coarse meal and the largest butter pieces are about 1/4 inch at their widest. Transfer to a #large bowl{}.

Add the buttermilk mixture to the flour mixture and fold with a #rubber spatula{} until just combined.

Transfer the dough to a floured work surface and knead until it just comes together, adding extra flour as necessary.

With a #rolling pin{}, roll the dough into a 12-inch square.

Using a #bench scraper{}, fold the right third of the dough over the center, then fold the left third over so you end up with a 12-by-4-inch rectangle. Fold the top third down over the center, then fold the bottom third up so the whole thing is reduced to a 4-inch square.

Press the square down and roll it out again into a 12-inch square. Repeat the folding process once more.

> To make Cheddar Cheese and Scallion Biscuits: In Step 9, sprinkle 6 oz grated cheddar cheese and 1/4 cup sliced scallions over the 12-inch dough square before folding it the second time, and continue as directed.

Roll the dough again into a 12-inch square.

Cut six 4-inch rounds out of the dough with a floured #biscuit cutter{}(4-inch). Transfer the rounds to a #parchment paper{}-lined #baking sheet{}, spacing them about 1 inch apart. Form the dough scraps into a ball and knead gently 2 or 3 times, until smooth. Roll the dough out until it's large enough to cut out 2 more 4-inch rounds, and transfer to the baking sheet.

Brush the tops of the biscuits with the @melted unsalted butter{28%g}.

Bake until golden brown and well risen, about ~bake{15%minutes}, rotating the pan halfway through.

Allow to cool for ~cool{5%minutes} and serve.
